    abstract = {Producing optimal left-deep trees is known to be NP-complete for general join graphs and a quite complex cost function counting disk accesses for a special block-wise nested-loop join [2]. Independent of any cost function is the dynamic programming approach to join ordering. The number of alternatives this approach generates is known as well [5]. Further, it is known that for some cost functions — those fulfilling the ASI property [4] — the problem can be solved in polynomial time for acyclic query graph, i.e., tree queries [2, 3].},
